WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, this is
really drawn in stark contrast

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
the difference between
people who have

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.237 line:92%
and the people who have not,

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one thing that I believe
is shocking to many,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wonder if you would have
predicted it,

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the fact that during this
terrible time,

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
billionaires have
actually added to their wealth

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a time when so many peopl
are living

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.084 size:78% position:39% line:92%
paycheck to paycheck.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, is this something that
of course Senator Sanders

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
knew would happen at a tim
like this?

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:28.228
-Well, I think not just me, bu
I think economists in general.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:31.598
We are -- and one of the issues,
Seth, that, you know,

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're not going to hear
too much in Congress or on TV,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:39.806
frankly, is the issue
of income and wealth inequality.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.341 line:92%
And as you have just indicated

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
it has been exasperated
by this crisis.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:48.581 line:92%
So we're seeing billionaires

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.150 line:92%
seeing their wealth increase

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.787 size:88% position:44%
by hundreds and hundreds
of billions of dollars,

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.990
while the most vulnerable
people in this country

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
and working-class people
in general

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.161 line:92%
are living in desperation.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, hunger in America
is now widespread.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.700
People are worried about being
evicted from their apartments.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where do they go?
What do they do?

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unemployment is higher now
than it has been

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:16.509 line:92%
for a very, very long time

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this issue of growing
income and wealth inequality

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the power
of the billionaire class

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.253 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to influence politics --

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.222 line:92%
they spend huge amounts of money

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
to elect candidates
who represent

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.025 line:92%
the wealthy and the powerful

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a fundamental issu
which we cannot run away from.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.400 line:92%
-Whether it's fair or unfair

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of people are
counting on you to convinc

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.939 size:84% position:42%
the progressive wing
of the Democratic Party

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to support Biden.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.708 size:84% position:42%
You've been very vocal
in your support of him.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:49.976 line:92%
Is he someone that you have ha

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
a good relationship
with over the years?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know your politics are
obviously different.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
But how do you like him
as a person?

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.053 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I have known Joe for --

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
since I got into
the Senate in 2006,

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:07.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
and worked with him when he wa
Vice President under Obama

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have a good relationship
with him.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, as you've indicated,
it is no great secret

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have
very different political views

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
Joe is more of an establishmen
politician,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm spending my life
taking on the establishment.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:25.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am going to do everythin
that I can

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:28.882 size:75% position:38%
to see that Biden is
elected president.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:34.354
Because in Trump, we have
not just somebody who is

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.922 size:75% position:38% line:92%
a pathological liar,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.791
but somebody who does not really
believe in democracy,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:42.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
who has very strong
authoritarian tendencies,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.831 line:92%
who is a racist and a sexist

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.232 line:92%
and a homophobe and a xenophobe.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:51.371
And this is somebody that cannot
be, in my view, re-elected

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the health and safety
of this country.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:56.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'll do everything I can to
support Joe and make sure

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.077 line:92%
that Trump is not re-elected

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Have you been happy thus fa
with the amount

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
former Vice President Bide
has reached out to you

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
and other progressives
in the party?

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, what he very
kindly did, what Joe did

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
is agree to a set
of task forces,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.463 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a half a dozen,

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are currently
wrapping up their work,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.034 size:81% position:41% line:92%
actually, as we speak,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
working on some of
the most important issues

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.871 size:78% position:39% line:92%
facing the country --

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:28.441
the economy, health care,
education, climate change,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
immigration, criminal justice,
et cetera.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Biden was very good
about reaching out.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have brought into these
task forces

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of the strongest
progressive voices in America.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.355 line:92%
He has strong supporters of his,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:48.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they are working on ways
that we can come up

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with real solutions

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:53.533 size:81% position:41%
to the enormous crises
facing this country.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.336 line:92%
And I've been pleased by that.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wanted to end
on some positive news

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.474 size:81% position:41%
because it's so hard
to come by these days.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Supreme Court ruled
6-3 yesterday

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.714
basically making it illega
for employers to fire someon

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on them being gay
or transgender.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you surprised, happy?
What was your reaction?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I was very happy.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:18.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very happy and a little
bit surprised.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's no great --

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.528 size:81% position:41%
everybody understands
that the conservatives

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.597 line:92%
dominate the Supreme Court 5-4

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:29.836
and that we had Gorsuch
and Roberts coming around

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this issue was very,
very pleasing.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:38.278
And I think as we fight fo
a less discriminatory societ

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we treat people as
who they are as human beings

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:45.752
not the color of their skin,
not their sexual orientation

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.986 line:92%
not where they were born.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:49.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a major, major, majo
step forward

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.324 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for the LGBT community

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:54.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think for
the United States of America

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I will say
what I said last time

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
we talked via Zoom.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope the next time's
in person.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So do I.
-And if not,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.169 line:92%
we will make it work this way.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a pleasure,
Senator.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.572 line:92%
-Keep up the great work, Seth.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
-Thank you.

